<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">29032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's parliament has filed a bill to withdraw from the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty — the agreement that gives international inspectors access to its nuclear sites.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>If the Guardian Council approves, Tehran would have ninety days to formally exit, compressing the timeline to a nuclear weapon from months to weeks.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The bill comes as US strikes continue to hit Iranian civilian sites, including a girls' school in Minab that a Pentagon investigation now admits likely killed a hundred and seventy-five people — the bombing campaign is producing the exact outcome it claimed to prevent.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>New videos verified by Bellingcat show Tomahawk missiles hit the Minab school compound in two separate waves — the second striking after first responders had already arrived.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Russia called a closed UN Security Council session Friday over the strike, but any formal statement requires US approval.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>All fifteen council members will meet, and the question is whether civilian accountability can survive a veto from the country that fired the missiles.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>After four weeks of silence, Yemen's Houthi forces launched ballistic missiles at Israeli targets Saturday, opening a second active front in the Iran war.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>They've warned they'll blockade Bab el-Mandeb, which carries ten percent of the world's oil — meaning both of the Middle East's critical shipping chokepoints could soon be closed simultaneously.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The USS Tripoli and twenty-five hundred Marines have arrived, and Washington is weighing whether to strike Yemen before that happens.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Saudi, Turkish, and Egyptian foreign ministers converged on Islamabad this week as Pakistan positions itself as the Muslim world's mediator in the Iran crisis.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Prime Minister Shehbaz spoke with Iran's President Pezeshkian for over an hour, relaying a fifteen-point US framework, while Islamabad simultaneously raised four hundred and twenty million dollars through Sukuk bonds as conventional credit markets froze.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Tehran's factions remain divided on whether to negotiate at all — and the fragile pause expires April sixth.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Twenty-five settler attacks hit the occupied West Bank in a single weekend, targeting villages from Jenin to Ramallah while the Israeli military's attention is fixed on Iran.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Settlers burned homes, a clinic, and a school — the Palestinian Red Crescent called the assault on Deir al-Hatab the most severe, with nine injured and no arrests.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Each regional escalation now provides cover for accelerated land seizure, and the pattern has become unmistakable.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Israeli airstrike hit a clearly marked press vehicle near Jezzine in southern Lebanon, killing three journalists — Al Mayadeen's Fatima Ftouni and her brother Mohammed, and Al-Manar's Ali Shuaib.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A second strike then targeted the paramedics who responded to the wreckage.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>No country in the Committee to Protect Journalists' recorded history has killed more journalists than Israel has in the past two years.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>While the world watches Iran, North Korea tested an upgraded solid-fuel ICBM engine designed to carry multiple warheads past US missile defenses.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Solid-fuel missiles need no pre-fueling, shrinking the detection window from hours to minutes.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Kim Jong Un told parliament that his country's nuclear status is irreversible — and with Washington consumed by the Middle East, no one is in a position to disagree.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia launched two hundred and seventy drones at Ukraine overnight, destroying a maternity ward in Odesa where twenty-two newborns had to be evacuated through rubble.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>With the world's attention locked on Iran, Moscow is intensifying strikes on civilian infrastructure across multiple cities with near-zero international response.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Secretary Rubio suggested this week that Ukrainian arms could be diverted to the Iran war — a signal that Kyiv may soon be fighting alone.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>French police arrested a seventeen-year-old outside a Bank of America branch in Paris, foiling what prosecutors are calling a terror attack.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>An Iran-linked Telegram channel had designated the branch a target days earlier, and the suspect was recruited via Snapchat for six hundred euros.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A second suspect remains at large as France heightens security around American interests — the war's reverberations are now reaching European streets.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>American gasoline has spiked a dollar per gallon in thirty days — the fastest rise since two thousand and eight.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> closure has cut ten million barrels per day from global supply, pushing Brent crude above a hundred and twenty dollars a barrel.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Analysts warn crude could reach a hundred and fifty if the strait stays closed, and the war that was supposed to be far away is now at every American gas pump.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Thirty-eight thousand tonnes of Indian petroleum reached Colombo harbour this week, pulling Sri Lanka back from the edge of a second economic collapse in four years.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The island imports all of its fuel, and the Hormuz closure had left it weeks from a repeat of the twenty twenty-two crisis that toppled a president.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Tehran is allowing Indian tankers through the strait, positioning New Delhi as the region's emergency fuel supplier and a quiet power broker.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iranian missiles and drones struck Emirates Global Aluminium's Al Taweelah plant in Abu Dhabi — the world's largest premium aluminium facility.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Workers were injured and the plant damaged; EGA supplies construction and electronics industries on every continent.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Tehran is now targeting Gulf industrial infrastructure, signaling that no economy in the region sits beyond the war's reach.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Göttingen have created gene-edited marmosets where every single cell carries the same genetic change — a clean knockout of otoferlin, the protein that transmits sound in the cochlea.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Previous CRISPR primate edits produced mosaics of edited and unedited cells, corrupting results and making the models scientifically unreliable.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Gene therapy for congenital deafness is already in pediatric trials, and this model may finally let researchers test it in an animal whose hearing mirrors our own.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Physicists in Vienna have proved that quantum events don't follow a fixed chronological order — a result eighteen standard deviations beyond what any causal explanation could produce.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A Bell-equivalent test confirmed temporal superposition as a fundamental property of quantum mechanics, not just a theoretical curiosity.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Loopholes remain, but the device already outperforms classical channels in cryptography — meaning the discovery is useful before it's fully understood.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>South Korea now requires solar panels on every public parking lot, turning dead asphalt into distributed power generation without consuming a single square metre of new land.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>At a hundred and twenty dollars a barrel, deploying renewables on existing infrastructure cuts payback time dramatically against building new power plants.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>It's the kind of policy that solves two problems at once — shade for cars, electricity for the grid.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt has given every medicine sold in the country a unique serial number, tracking it from factory to pharmacy shelf.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The system launched earlier this month to combat counterfeits that kill hundreds of thousands across Africa annually.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>But experts warn sixty percent of fake drugs enter through informal channels the system can't reach — a familiar gap between digital ambition and markets that still run on handshakes and cash.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>